WEBVTT


00:01:13.407 --> 00:01:15.909
<i>There are gajillions of stories...</i>


00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:18.120
<i>of mischief and fun,</i>


00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:20.080
<i>but to keep things simple,</i>


00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:22.791
<i>let's start with just one...</i>


00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.419
<i>about a mom and two kids...</i>


00:01:25.502 --> 00:01:27.713
<i>and a house and a hat...</i>


00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:29.715
<i>that, oddly enough,</i>


00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:32.092
<i>was worn by a cat.</i>


00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:36.180
<i>But soon enough
we will get to all that.</i>


00:01:36.305 --> 00:01:40.184
<i>In the valley that stretches
from this hill to that hill,</i>


00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:42.311
<i>a city is nestled...</i>


00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:45.480
<i>that city is Anville.</i>


00:01:45.606 --> 00:01:47.816
- Hurry up!
We'll miss the movie!
- Any more tutti-frutti?


00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:48.901
I'll check.
Thanks!


00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:53.197
<i>It's a town that's not huge,
but quite big enough...</i>


00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.491
<i>for buyers and sellers
to sell and buy stuff,</i>


00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:59.286
<i>from shoes and shirts...</i>


00:01:59.411 --> 00:02:01.580
<i>and elongated ladders...</i>


00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:05.918
<i>to sailboats and gibble-grated
berry-juice bladders.</i>


00:02:07.503 --> 00:02:12.883
<i>So our story begins
at the corner
of Main and Montroob...</i>


00:02:13.008 --> 00:02:15.385
<i>in the spotless
real estate office...</i>


00:02:15.511 --> 00:02:19.097
<i>run by Hank Humberfloob.</i>


00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:22.893
<i>Humberfloob Real Estate. How can
we make your dreams come true?</i>


00:02:29.608 --> 00:02:30.984
What do you mean,
you're leaving?


00:02:31.109 --> 00:02:34.488
You're a babysitter.
Babysitters don't leave. They sit.


00:02:34.613 --> 00:02:37.491
Baby-leavers leave.
I'm sorry. I really
gotta go, Miss Walden.


00:02:37.616 --> 00:02:40.494
Well, I need to come home
right away.


00:02:40.619 --> 00:02:43.205
All right.
Thank you, Amy.
Sorry.


00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:49.711
Attention, everyone!
It's 9:02.


00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.005
Staff meeting!
Staff meeting!


00:02:52.089 --> 00:02:55.092
<i>Look alive, everyone!</i>


00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:57.219
First I'd like to
welcome aboard...


00:02:57.386 --> 00:03:00.514
our newest member
of the Humberfloob family,


00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:02.808
Jim McFlinnagan!


00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:04.685
- Mr. Humberfloob,
I wanted to thank you...


00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.812
Fired.
I beg your pardon?


00:03:06.895 --> 00:03:09.314
Fired.
B-But l...


00:03:09.398 --> 00:03:13.610
Fired!


00:03:16.488 --> 00:03:19.491
One, two, three,
four, five, six, seven,
eight, nine, 10!


00:03:21.994 --> 00:03:25.998
As you know, tonight is
our bimonthly “meet and greet" party.


00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:29.585
Tonight's host is...
Joan Walden.


00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:33.714
This is where people can
meet our real estate agents...


00:03:33.797 --> 00:03:37.718
in an informal,
yet hygienic setting.


00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.804
Mr. Humberfloob,
I have to get home to my kids.


00:03:42.181 --> 00:03:44.183
Ah, yes.


00:03:45.517 --> 00:03:48.020
Your children.


00:03:48.103 --> 00:03:52.316
Joan, let me make this
perfectly clear.


00:03:52.399 --> 00:03:57.112
If your house
is as messy as last time,


00:03:57.196 --> 00:04:00.199
you're fired!


00:04:02.284 --> 00:04:05.913
That's pretty clear,
Mr. Humberfloob.


00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:07.915
Don't worry. I promise.


00:04:07.998 --> 00:04:10.417
My kids'll be
on their best behavior.


00:04:11.293 --> 00:04:13.212
Great.


00:04:14.713 --> 00:04:17.090
<i>Humberfloob Real Estate.</i>


00:04:17.216 --> 00:04:20.093
<i>How can we make
your dreams come true?
Please hold.</i>


00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:24.181
<i>If you leave Humberfloob's
and turn left onto Main,</i>


00:04:24.306 --> 00:04:28.810
<i>three miles down
you'll find Lipplapper Lane,</i>


00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:32.314
<i>a pleasant-enough street
in a pleasant-enough way...</i>


00:04:32.481 --> 00:04:36.818
<i>where a neighbor greeted neighbor
with a neighborly "Hey!"</i>


00:04:36.902 --> 00:04:38.403
Hey!
Hey!


00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:42.783
<i>Here the hedges were hedged,
the weeds were all weeded,</i>


00:04:42.908 --> 00:04:45.285
<i>and lawns were mowed daily,</i>


00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:48.288
<i>twice daily if needed.</i>


00:04:48.413 --> 00:04:50.582
<i>And at the end
of this street,</i>


00:04:50.707 --> 00:04:52.918
<i>in a house like any other,</i>


00:04:53.001 --> 00:04:55.087
<i>something magical
would happen...</i>


00:04:55.212 --> 00:04:58.298
<i>to a sister and her brother.</i>


00:05:07.516 --> 00:05:10.310
<i>Shh! Nevins!
Stealth mode.</i>


00:05:10.394 --> 00:05:12.312
Today's to-do list.


00:05:12.396 --> 00:05:14.815
Number one:
Make to-do list.


00:05:14.898 --> 00:05:17.192
Number two:
Practice coloring.


00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:20.112
Number three:
Research graduate schools.


00:05:20.112 --> 00:05:22.906
Number four:
Be spontaneous.


00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.493
Number five:
Create lasting
childhood memories.


00:05:26.493 --> 00:05:29.788
<i>And number six:
Amend will.</i>


00:05:31.081 --> 00:05:33.417
What is he doing?


00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:54.313
Number 10:
Make tomorrow's to-do list.


00:05:57.816 --> 00:06:00.319
<i>Ladies and gentlemen!</i>


00:06:00.402 --> 00:06:02.196
Nevins,
your attention, please.


00:06:02.321 --> 00:06:05.282
You are about to witness
the third most spectacular stunt...


00:06:05.407 --> 00:06:07.784
ever performed
under this roof!


00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:11.496
Do you know how hard it's getting
to tell people that we're related?


00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:15.083
Relax.
I'll put everything back.


00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:27.804
And now,
for the indoor stair luge!


00:06:27.888 --> 00:06:29.806
Indoor stair luge?


00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:32.100
I'll have to add this one
to my list.


00:06:32.184 --> 00:06:34.895
Go have no fun
somewhere else.


00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.482
<i>It... is... showtime!</i>


00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:43.487
<i>Whoa!</i>


00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:48.784
- Aah!
- Yeah!


00:06:50.494 --> 00:06:53.080
<i>- Oh, my word!</i>


00:06:53.205 --> 00:06:55.082
Nevins!


00:06:55.207 --> 00:06:58.502
<i>Nevins, come back!</i>


00:07:00.003 --> 00:07:01.880
Hey, Mom. What's up?


00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:08.387
You are so lucky
you didn't ruin this dress.


00:07:08.512 --> 00:07:11.014
Mom, I know
you're angry,


00:07:11.098 --> 00:07:13.016
but there's something
you need to know.


00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.686
This was all Sally's fault.
Oh, really?


00:07:15.811 --> 00:07:18.188
And how, exactly,
was it Sally's fault?


00:07:18.313 --> 00:07:20.315
Give me a minute.
I'm workin' on it.


00:07:20.399 --> 00:07:22.818
Save it, Conrad.


00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:25.988
Why today? Why did you
have to pick today
to destroy the house?


00:07:26.113 --> 00:07:27.990
You know
what's happening today.


00:07:28.115 --> 00:07:29.992
I tried to tell him, Mom.


00:07:30.117 --> 00:07:32.494
"Mom's throwing
a very important party," I said.


00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:34.496
"All other important
clients will be here."


00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:38.292
But he went right ahead
and wrecked the house
and let Nevins get away.


00:07:38.417 --> 00:07:41.003
Now, again, I hope
you're going to ground him.


00:07:41.086 --> 00:07:43.797
Yes, Sally, for a week, but
that's none of your business.


00:07:43.881 --> 00:07:45.799
A week?
Come on. Two days.


00:07:45.883 --> 00:07:48.302
I asked you to do
one thing today, Conrad...


00:07:48.385 --> 00:07:50.304
keep the house
clean.


00:07:50.512 --> 00:07:55.309
Do you know how frustrating it is
that you're always doing
the exact opposite of what I say?


00:07:55.809 --> 00:07:57.519
<i>Knock, knock, knock.</i>


00:07:57.603 --> 00:07:59.813
Someone lose a dog?


00:07:59.897 --> 00:08:01.815
<i>I found him next door...</i>


00:08:01.899 --> 00:08:03.817
in my yard... again.


00:08:03.901 --> 00:08:06.320
You are a saint.


00:08:06.403 --> 00:08:09.198
And here I thought
you were only dating me
for my good looks.


00:08:09.281 --> 00:08:11.700
Lucky us.
Larry Quinn is here.


00:08:11.783 --> 00:08:14.912
<i>Hey-a, sport.
Call me Lawrence.
Okay?</i>


00:08:14.995 --> 00:08:17.998
You rescued Nevins!
Thanks, Lawrence!


00:08:18.081 --> 00:08:20.918
It was my pleasure, Sally.
Anything for my little princess.


00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:22.586
Oh, I don't wanna be a princess.


00:08:22.711 --> 00:08:26.381
In a constitutional monarchy
parliament has all the real power.


00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:29.718
I see.
Okay, that's great.


00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:31.887
Uh, look, pal, be a sport.


00:08:32.012 --> 00:08:35.891
<i>Why don't you go
tidy up the living room.
Okay...dude?</i>


00:08:36.016 --> 00:08:37.809
I don't have to listen to you, Larry.


00:08:37.893 --> 00:08:40.187
Conrad,
do what Lawrence says.


00:08:53.283 --> 00:08:57.204
Have you given some thought
about the Wilhelm Academy?


00:08:57.287 --> 00:09:00.415
You mean the Colonel Wilhelm
Military Academy for Troubled Youth?


00:09:00.582 --> 00:09:03.001
That's the one, Joan.


00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:06.296
I'm not sure
it's right for Conrad.


00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:09.883
Oh, Joan, Joan.


00:09:10.008 --> 00:09:12.511
Joan, Joan, Joan.


00:09:13.595 --> 00:09:16.306
I have so much respect
for you, Joan.


00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:20.018
Single mother, career woman,
raising two children on your own,


00:09:20.102 --> 00:09:24.398
and still finding time
to be the best darned
real estate agent in town.


00:09:26.316 --> 00:09:28.819
I know how hard it is, Joan.


00:09:28.902 --> 00:09:32.489
It is hard.
Oh... I know.


00:09:32.698 --> 00:09:35.617
<i>And I know
how hard you're trying.</i>


00:09:37.411 --> 00:09:40.080
This is a once-in-a-lifetime
proposition,
and you must act now.


00:09:40.205 --> 00:09:43.083
The Colonel Wilhelm
Military Academy
for Troubled Youth...


00:09:43.208 --> 00:09:46.003
is what we call in the sales game
a win-win scenario.


00:09:46.086 --> 00:09:50.799
A top-flight military school,
and it's only... eight hours away.


00:09:52.801 --> 00:09:56.096
<i>Oh, the phone.</i>


00:10:04.396 --> 00:10:06.315
I heard what you said.


00:10:06.398 --> 00:10:08.317
I'm not going to military school, Larry.


00:10:08.483 --> 00:10:10.903
Look, buddy,


00:10:10.986 --> 00:10:13.906
I know I'm not your dad...


00:10:13.989 --> 00:10:16.909
and this is probably
really strange for you...


00:10:16.992 --> 00:10:18.702
your neighbor's
dating your mom.


00:10:18.702 --> 00:10:22.289
But here's the thing, son.
Come here.


00:10:22.414 --> 00:10:24.791
I don't like you either.


00:10:24.917 --> 00:10:27.503
But I'm gonna
marry your mom.


00:10:27.586 --> 00:10:31.798
And if it was up to me,
you'd be at military school today.


00:10:31.882 --> 00:10:34.301
I'm not going
to military school.
Ohh!


00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.386
I think you're gonna love it.


00:10:36.512 --> 00:10:38.388
It's just like summer camp,


00:10:38.514 --> 00:10:40.390
except with brutal forced marches...


00:10:40.516 --> 00:10:42.392
and soul-crushing discipline.


00:10:42.518 --> 00:10:47.105
And one more thing...
It's Lawrence,
you snot-nosed son of a...


00:10:47.189 --> 00:10:50.108
wonderful woman
who I'm absolutely crazy about!
Oww!


00:10:50.192 --> 00:10:52.110
Gosh, I love children!


00:10:52.194 --> 00:10:54.112
Oh, Joan,
I didn't see you there.


00:10:54.196 --> 00:10:56.907
Would you be a doll
and help me bring up chairs
from the basement?


00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.618
Nothing would give me
more pleasure, Joan,
but I do have to run.


00:10:59.618 --> 00:11:02.496
I have a very important
sales conference downtown.


00:11:02.496 --> 00:11:04.915
Oh. Okay.


00:11:04.998 --> 00:11:07.709
- Well, I'll see you at the party tonight.
- Sure.


00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:33.110
Mom, that guy's a total phony.
You can't let Larry...


00:11:33.193 --> 00:11:36.113
<i>It's Lawrence, Conrad.</i>


00:11:36.905 --> 00:11:39.408
Kate's Catering.
I'm here to do your party tonight.


00:11:39.491 --> 00:11:42.119
Oh, hi.
Where's Kate?


00:11:42.202 --> 00:11:45.289
I'm Kate.
Oh. Okay.


00:11:45.414 --> 00:11:47.291
Right this way, Kate.


00:11:47.416 --> 00:11:49.001
<i>Mom, you've gotta
listen to me...</i>


00:11:49.084 --> 00:11:51.503
Quiet!
Two weeks ago
you said you would...


00:11:51.712 --> 00:11:53.881
I "specialed" it.
See?


00:11:54.006 --> 00:11:57.092
Quiet!
Nevins!


00:11:57.217 --> 00:11:59.219
I said quiet!


00:12:02.806 --> 00:12:06.894
Joan Walden Real Estate.
Be it ever so humble,
there's no place like Joan.


00:12:07.019 --> 00:12:09.104
This is Mr. Humberfloob.


00:12:09.188 --> 00:12:12.983
- Oh, hi, Mr. Humberfloob.
- Joan, I need you to come back to the office.


00:12:13.108 --> 00:12:15.402
<i>- Today?
- Yes, Joan.</i>


00:12:15.485 --> 00:12:18.113
- No problem?
- No problem at all.


00:12:18.197 --> 00:12:20.115
Great!


00:12:20.199 --> 00:12:22.618
- What's going on, Mommy?


00:12:22.701 --> 00:12:26.497
Mommy has to go
back to the office.


00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:29.291
Oh! I hope Mrs. Kwan
can baby-sit.


00:12:29.416 --> 00:12:32.002
<i>- Not Mrs. Kwan!</i>


00:12:34.296 --> 00:12:36.215
Oh!
Hi, Mrs. Kwan.


00:12:36.298 --> 00:12:38.217
Hi.
I'm running late.


00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:41.220
Thanks for babysitting
on such short notice.
Mmm, yeah.


00:12:41.303 --> 00:12:43.305
Okay, Mrs. Kwan.


00:12:43.388 --> 00:12:44.806
Oh-oh-oh!


00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:47.601
I'll be back
in a couple of hours.
Hi.


00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:50.312
<i>Conrad's grounded,
so no video games.</i>


00:12:50.521 --> 00:12:52.397
<i>Sally?
Last chance.</i>


00:12:52.481 --> 00:12:55.484
If you wanna make cupcakes,
I can take you to
your friend Ginny's house.


00:12:55.609 --> 00:12:57.486
<i>- Ginny's not my friend anymore.</i>


00:12:57.611 --> 00:13:00.280
<i>Last time we made cupcakes
she wanted to be the head chef.</i>


00:13:00.405 --> 00:13:02.282
<i>I'm the head chef.</i>


00:13:02.407 --> 00:13:04.117
What about Denise, then?


00:13:04.201 --> 00:13:06.995
She talked back to me,
so I ordered her
not to speak to me anymore.


00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:10.207
- And you don't like bossy?
- I won't tolerate it.


00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.917
Right.


00:13:11.917 --> 00:13:14.795
Well, if you're both staying,
remember the rules.


00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:18.006
Conrad: No playing ball
in the house, no fighting,


00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:20.008
no answering the phone,
"City morgue."


00:13:20.092 --> 00:13:22.010
Mommy,
can't I have some rules?


00:13:23.595 --> 00:13:25.597
No chewing tobacco.


00:13:25.681 --> 00:13:27.683
Thanks, Mom.
You have my word.


00:13:27.808 --> 00:13:33.105
And absolutely no one
sets foot in the living room, or else.


00:13:33.188 --> 00:13:36.817
<i>Or else what?
You're gonna do what Larry said
and send me to military school?</i>


00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:40.320
Maybe if you'd just behave,
I wouldn't have to consider military school.


00:13:40.404 --> 00:13:42.406
I wish I could trust you.


00:13:43.991 --> 00:13:45.993
I wish I had a different mom.


00:13:46.118 --> 00:13:49.496
Well, sometimes
I wish the same thing.


00:14:05.512 --> 00:14:07.389
Mmm.


00:14:12.811 --> 00:14:15.189
Good luck with your meeting.


00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:41.798
<i>Children, would you like
to watch television with me?</i>


00:14:41.882 --> 00:14:46.303
<i>- We don't have to tell your mother.</i>


00:14:53.685 --> 00:14:56.813
<i>Taiwanese parliament.</i>


00:14:56.897 --> 00:15:00.609
<i>You tell them, Kwi-Chang!
No more big government!</i>


00:15:00.817 --> 00:15:02.486
<i>Rip his heart out!</i>


00:15:15.499 --> 00:15:17.709
Hit me!


00:15:20.003 --> 00:15:22.381
<i>So they slumped in their chairs,</i>


00:15:22.506 --> 00:15:24.591
<i>too glum to complain,</i>


00:15:24.591 --> 00:15:28.220
<i>and to make matters worse,
it started to rain.</i>


00:15:31.598 --> 00:15:33.517
<i>They sat in the house...</i>


00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:36.019
<i>on that cold, cold, wet day...</i>


00:15:36.186 --> 00:15:38.105
<i>with no fun to have...</i>


00:15:38.188 --> 00:15:40.107
<i>and no games to play.</i>


00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:42.192
<i>They could just
stare out the window...</i>


00:15:42.317 --> 00:15:44.486
<i>or perhaps get a nap in,</i>


00:15:44.611 --> 00:15:46.780
<i>and hope that something,</i>


00:15:46.905 --> 00:15:48.782
<i>anything might happen.</i>


00:15:48.907 --> 00:15:50.492
Quit bothering
the fish.


00:15:50.617 --> 00:15:52.995
I know.
Quit bothering the fish.


00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.496
Spit hand!
Oh, gross!


00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:59.001
Get that away from me!
Get it away!


00:15:59.084 --> 00:16:01.587
<i>Then something went bump.</i>


00:16:01.712 --> 00:16:03.505
- What was that?


00:16:03.589 --> 00:16:06.884
<i>How that bump
made them jump.</i>


00:16:07.009 --> 00:16:10.220
<i>I think it came
from the closet.</i>


00:16:41.919 --> 00:16:43.795
Conrad?


00:16:43.921 --> 00:16:46.215
Conrad.


00:16:47.299 --> 00:16:49.801
Come on, Conrad.


00:16:55.307 --> 00:16:57.184
You shouldn't scare people.


00:16:57.309 --> 00:17:00.312
You should've seen
the look on your face.
It was like you saw a monster...


00:17:00.395 --> 00:17:02.689
A monster? Where?


00:17:04.691 --> 00:17:07.986
That could've gone better.


00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.619
<i>What was that?
I don't know.</i>


00:17:15.786 --> 00:17:17.913
<i>Looked like
a humongous cat.</i>


00:17:18.997 --> 00:17:20.207
"Humongous"?


00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:23.794
