00:32:53.807 --> 00:32:55.684
Hmm?


00:32:55.809 --> 00:32:58.520
Now, close the lid
and Bob's your flippin' uncle!


00:32:58.604 --> 00:33:00.397
What an
astounding product!


00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:01.982
<i>Oh, yeah!</i>


00:33:02.107 --> 00:33:04.902
Open the drawer,


00:33:04.985 --> 00:33:08.697
<i>Fill the patented
Kupkake-inator tray,</i>


00:33:08.780 --> 00:33:11.617
<i>- Close the drawer,</i>


00:33:11.700 --> 00:33:14.912
Then place it
in a conventional oven.


00:33:19.583 --> 00:33:22.002
Delicious cupcakes
are just minutes away.


00:33:22.085 --> 00:33:24.004
Did you just say
"minutes away"?


00:33:24.087 --> 00:33:25.714
That's impossible!


00:33:25.797 --> 00:33:29.009
You're not just wrong,
you're stupid.
Now, wait just a minute...


00:33:29.218 --> 00:33:31.094
And you're ugly,
just like your mum.


00:33:31.303 --> 00:33:33.680
<i>Did you just call
my mother ugly?</i>


00:33:33.889 --> 00:33:36.391
Shut up! I mean it!
I will end you!


00:33:38.519 --> 00:33:41.104
Um, Cat.
Your tail.


00:33:41.188 --> 00:33:43.815
What about it?


00:33:43.899 --> 00:33:48.320
Oh, I see! I've chopped it off.
That's interesting, because...


00:33:49.613 --> 00:33:52.783
Son of a bi...


00:33:55.702 --> 00:33:58.580
Look, I'm not saying
we're going to sue.


00:33:58.789 --> 00:34:00.999
I'm just saying
we have a case.


00:34:01.083 --> 00:34:03.001
We'll talk later.
Ixnay, ixnay.


00:34:03.085 --> 00:34:05.420
Hi.


00:34:05.504 --> 00:34:08.090
Cat, is the oven
supposed to be
making that sound?


00:34:08.215 --> 00:34:10.092
Huh?


00:34:10.217 --> 00:34:13.387
Of course. That means
they're almost done, Conrack.


00:34:13.512 --> 00:34:15.597
- Conrad.
- That's what I said, Condor.


00:34:15.681 --> 00:34:18.183
<i>- Cat!
- Now, that's my name!</i>


00:34:25.816 --> 00:34:28.110
<i>Yep!</i>


00:34:28.193 --> 00:34:30.112
They're done!


00:34:30.320 --> 00:34:32.698
Oh, man!
There's nothing
to worry about.


00:34:32.781 --> 00:34:34.700
I'm sure
they still taste fine.


00:34:34.783 --> 00:34:36.702
Yecch!
They're horrible!


00:34:36.785 --> 00:34:39.997
Who wants some?
Come on, come on!


00:34:41.081 --> 00:34:43.000
Oh... my... cod.


00:34:43.083 --> 00:34:44.501
Ohh! Aah!


00:34:44.585 --> 00:34:47.504
Cat, you need to
clean this mess up pronto.


00:34:47.588 --> 00:34:50.799
We have a contract.
All right, I'll try.


00:34:52.301 --> 00:34:55.012
You don't try. You do.


00:34:55.095 --> 00:34:58.015
Yes, ma'am.
Right away, ma'am.


00:34:58.098 --> 00:35:00.809
I'll be right back.


00:35:00.893 --> 00:35:02.686
<i>Whoa!</i>


00:35:05.898 --> 00:35:08.192
Hi.
How are ya?


00:35:08.317 --> 00:35:10.319
Okay.


00:35:13.405 --> 00:35:15.616
Look. I'm a girl.


00:35:19.286 --> 00:35:21.413
Stop! That's...


00:35:21.497 --> 00:35:23.081
Mom's dress!


00:35:23.207 --> 00:35:26.585
This filthy thing?


00:35:26.710 --> 00:35:28.795
She was gonna wear that tonight,
and you ruined it.


00:35:28.921 --> 00:35:31.882
Honey, it was ruined
when she bought it.


00:35:33.091 --> 00:35:35.010
Mm-hmm. Yeah.
Mm-hmm.


00:35:35.093 --> 00:35:38.013
<i>I told you
all this would happen!</i>


00:35:38.096 --> 00:35:41.099
- But no one listens to a fish!
- Oy.


00:35:41.183 --> 00:35:43.810
<i>A dog goes "woof-woof"
and everybody knows that
little Timmy's trapped under a log.</i>


00:35:43.894 --> 00:35:45.687
<i>But a fish speaks
in plain English...</i>


00:35:45.896 --> 00:35:46.480
All right, everyone,
let's just take a deep breath
and calm down.


00:35:52.611 --> 00:35:56.198
<i>You know who's gonna solve it?
Me. I am.</i>


00:35:56.281 --> 00:35:59.201
I will personally
take care of everything.


00:36:00.494 --> 00:36:02.412
And I know
just the guys to do it.


00:36:16.093 --> 00:36:19.680
In this box are two Things.
I will show them to you.


00:36:19.805 --> 00:36:24.017
<i>Two Things, and I call them
Thing One and Thing Two.</i>


00:36:24.101 --> 00:36:27.479
These Things will not bite you.
They want to have fun.


00:36:27.604 --> 00:36:29.690
So without further ado,


00:36:29.815 --> 00:36:33.110
meet Thing Two
and Thing One!


00:36:35.612 --> 00:36:37.489
@Ta-da @


00:36:37.614 --> 00:36:40.409
Oh, yeah!


00:36:40.492 --> 00:36:43.620
Thing One, Conrad, Sally.
Conrad, Sally, Thing One.


00:36:43.787 --> 00:36:45.706
<i>Thing Two, Conrad, Sally.
Conrad, Sally, Thing Two.</i>


00:36:45.914 --> 00:36:49.001
Thing One, Thing Two.
Thing Two, Thing One.
Conrad, Sally. Sally, Conrad.


00:36:49.209 --> 00:36:51.712
I am the Cat.
Don't belittle me.


00:36:51.920 --> 00:36:53.797
Ah, yes, of course.


00:36:53.881 --> 00:36:56.800
Thing Two would like to
clarify that just because
he wears the number two...


00:36:56.884 --> 00:36:59.386
does not imply in any way
that he's inferior to Thing One.


00:36:59.511 --> 00:37:00.804
And all of the above.


00:37:00.888 --> 00:37:04.516
He says you may feel free
to call him Thing "A," if you like.


00:37:04.600 --> 00:37:07.895
He will also accept Super Thing,
Thing King, Kid Dynamite,


00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:10.689
Chocolate Thun-Da...
or Ben.
 Ben!


00:37:13.483 --> 00:37:16.403
Thing One says
he's Thing One for a reason,


00:37:16.487 --> 00:37:18.906
and some people
should just get used to it.


00:37:18.989 --> 00:37:21.617
It's a Thing thing.
You wouldn't understand.


00:37:21.700 --> 00:37:24.119
Okay, enough!


00:37:24.203 --> 00:37:26.413
You are quickly turning into
one of my least favorite Things.


00:37:28.081 --> 00:37:31.001
Listen, Convex,
you probably don't
wanna do that.


00:37:31.084 --> 00:37:33.003
Why not?
It's just a crate.


00:37:33.086 --> 00:37:34.505
This isn't just any old crate.


00:37:34.588 --> 00:37:37.716
It's the Trans-dimensional
Transportolator.


00:37:37.799 --> 00:37:41.011
It's kinda like a doorway
which leads from this world
to my world.


00:37:41.094 --> 00:37:43.388
But it says,
"Made in the Philippines."


00:37:43.514 --> 00:37:46.683
<i>Yes, but not this Philippines.</i>


00:37:46.808 --> 00:37:51.313
<i>Look, now,
I'm not usually a rules guy,
but this is a biggie.</i>


00:37:51.396 --> 00:37:53.398
No opening the crate.


00:37:53.482 --> 00:37:56.485
No lookee, no touchee.
Got it?


00:37:56.693 --> 00:37:59.696
<i>Mekka-dekka we should
settle our differences.</i>


00:38:03.617 --> 00:38:05.494
<i>Things, front and center!</i>


00:38:05.619 --> 00:38:07.412
Cool.


00:38:07.496 --> 00:38:11.291
All right, Things,
I'm not paying you to
stand around and look pretty.


00:38:11.416 --> 00:38:13.418
<i>Here's Mom's dress.</i>


00:38:13.502 --> 00:38:15.420
<i>Oh! Mommy's dress!</i>


00:38:19.716 --> 00:38:22.511
- What about the couch?
- Which couch?


00:38:22.594 --> 00:38:24.596
<i>The clean one,
or the horribly stained one?</i>


00:38:33.605 --> 00:38:36.191
Ho!


00:38:36.316 --> 00:38:38.193
Mekka-dekka
don't worry!


00:38:39.611 --> 00:38:41.780
Incoming!


00:38:44.116 --> 00:38:48.787
<i>Cat, they're wrecking
the whole house!</i>


00:39:09.016 --> 00:39:12.895
- Conrad, help!
- Help yourself!


00:39:13.020 --> 00:39:15.898
Look at me!
Come and get it!


00:39:21.403 --> 00:39:25.616
Whoa! Ooh, yeah! Whoa!


00:39:33.582 --> 00:39:35.584
That tickles!


00:39:36.919 --> 00:39:39.796
Geronimo!


00:39:42.799 --> 00:39:46.512
Mine, mine, mine!
Mine, mine, mine, mine, mine!


00:39:47.888 --> 00:39:51.183
Ride 'em, cowboy!
Yee-hee-hee! Ho-ho-ho! Whee!


00:39:59.399 --> 00:40:01.610
If this were my house,
I'd be furious.


00:40:08.408 --> 00:40:11.286
Hey! Klondike!


00:40:11.411 --> 00:40:15.082
Do you have any idea
what happened to the lock
on this crate?


00:40:15.207 --> 00:40:17.584
- It's on Nevins's collar.
- Nevins?


00:40:17.709 --> 00:40:19.419
<i>Nevins? Nevins!</i>


00:40:19.503 --> 00:40:23.507
Put the dog down!
I said, put the dog down!


00:40:23.590 --> 00:40:25.509
Why won't they
listen to me?


00:40:25.592 --> 00:40:31.181
Oh. I don't know if this helps,
but the Things always do
the opposite of what you say.


00:40:31.306 --> 00:40:34.810
Why do they always
do the opposite?
That's so annoying!


00:40:34.893 --> 00:40:36.812
Remind you of anyone,
Conrad?


00:40:36.895 --> 00:40:39.481
<i>Zinga!</i>


00:40:39.690 --> 00:40:41.608
Zinga! Zinga!


00:40:41.817 --> 00:40:44.695
Blue! 41! Set!
Hut! Hut! Hut! Hut!


00:40:44.820 --> 00:40:48.615
Hey, Thing,
don't let go of that dog!


00:40:48.699 --> 00:40:50.409
Let go!


00:40:50.492 --> 00:40:54.121
<i>Catch him...
I mean, don't catch him!</i>


00:40:57.291 --> 00:40:58.584
Well, this is just great, Conrad.


00:40:58.709 --> 00:41:02.796
The whole house is destroyed,
the party is ruined,
and now Nevins is gone.


00:41:02.880 --> 00:41:05.299
Sally, Kojak,


00:41:05.382 --> 00:41:09.511
that's nothing compared
to what's gonna happen
if we don't lock this crate.


00:41:09.720 --> 00:41:12.598
Take a look.
It's already leaking.


00:41:16.310 --> 00:41:19.813
- It won't stay shut.
- Not without the lock.


00:41:19.897 --> 00:41:24.818
Look, if we don't get that lock off of Nevins
and put it back on this crate,


00:41:24.902 --> 00:41:28.697
we're gonna be staring down
the business end
of the mother of all messes.


00:41:29.990 --> 00:41:32.910
We've gotta go out
and find Nevins.


00:41:32.993 --> 00:41:35.287
Impossible! Sally!


00:41:35.412 --> 00:41:37.789
<i>There's only four hours
till the party.</i>


00:41:37.915 --> 00:41:40.417
The Fish is right.
We should call Mom
and tell her what happened.


00:41:40.501 --> 00:41:43.712
Look at this house!
There's no way we could
explain this to Mom.


00:41:43.921 --> 00:41:46.507
We gotta get Nevins back
and lock the crate!


00:41:46.715 --> 00:41:48.592
We're staying and calling Mom.


00:41:48.717 --> 00:41:51.011
We're going and getting the dog.


00:41:51.094 --> 00:41:53.180
There is a third option.


00:41:53.305 --> 00:41:55.599
<i>There is?</i>


00:41:55.682 --> 00:41:59.102
<i>Yes. It involves...</i>


00:41:59.186 --> 00:42:01.188
murder!


00:42:01.313 --> 00:42:04.191
- That's your option?
- No.


00:42:04.316 --> 00:42:07.110
But you guys both had options.
I just wanted to have one too.


00:42:07.194 --> 00:42:10.489
Or did I?


00:42:10.614 --> 00:42:14.409
- Cat, you're not helping!
- Come on. Let's go get that dog.


00:42:14.493 --> 00:42:18.997
<i>Now, we just need
a heavy, inanimate object
to weigh down this crate.</i>


00:42:25.003 --> 00:42:27.506
There. That oughta
buy us some time.


00:42:27.589 --> 00:42:31.593
Come on, kids!
Let's go, go, go!


00:42:36.098 --> 00:42:38.892
<i>Identical sister Mitzy...</i>


00:42:39.017 --> 00:42:42.104
<i>That's right.</i>


00:42:46.191 --> 00:42:48.902
<i>- Yeah!</i>


00:42:50.696 --> 00:42:52.614
What do you want now?


00:42:52.698 --> 00:42:55.284
Repo.


00:42:55.409 --> 00:42:58.620
You're repossessing my TV?


00:42:58.704 --> 00:43:00.080
I'm sure I made a payment.


00:43:00.080 --> 00:43:03.000
If it's about that bounced check,
let me give you a credit card.


00:43:03.083 --> 00:43:07.504
That one's expired.
Huh? Oh, come on!


00:43:09.715 --> 00:43:13.886
<i>With the lock on his collar,
Nevins kept running,</i>


00:43:14.011 --> 00:43:16.388
<i>unaware of his part...</i>


00:43:16.513 --> 00:43:19.016
<i>in the evil Quinn's cunning.</i>


00:43:19.099 --> 00:43:22.102
Joan Walden Real Estate.
Be it ever so humble, there's no...


00:43:22.186 --> 00:43:23.812
Oh, hi, Joan.


00:43:23.896 --> 00:43:26.398
The kids let the dog
out again.
You're kidding.


00:43:26.607 --> 00:43:30.319
Don't worry. I'll go get him,
then we'll have a conversation
vis-a-vis military school.


00:43:30.402 --> 00:43:33.780
I don't know.
Conrad's like you, Lawrence.


00:43:33.989 --> 00:43:36.783
He's very... sensitive.
Uh-huh.


00:43:36.909 --> 00:43:39.912
But I suppose it's something
I should consider.


00:43:39.995 --> 00:43:43.290
I'll get the dog.
I'll be right over.


00:43:50.881 --> 00:43:53.300
<i>Okay, there's Nevins.</i>


00:43:53.383 --> 00:43:56.803
<i>Stay out of sight.</i>


00:44:08.899 --> 00:44:11.485
I thought the moment
needed something.


00:44:11.610 --> 00:44:14.279
Oh, what will become of us?


00:44:14.404 --> 00:44:16.490
Your mother will lose her job,


00:44:16.615 --> 00:44:19.910
and we'll have to...
live on the street!


00:44:19.993 --> 00:44:23.080
I can't! Don't make me go...


00:44:23.205 --> 00:44:25.582
<i>I don't know this world!</i>


00:44:25.707 --> 00:44:30.504
It's dry! It's like...
I can't... It's too...
Fish!


00:44:30.587 --> 00:44:32.506
It's too much!


00:44:32.589 --> 00:44:34.591
Would you like to go back
in the toilet?


00:44:34.716 --> 00:44:37.219
On second thought,
it's such a beautiful day.
Why spend it indoors?


00:44:37.302 --> 00:44:40.013
- Thank you!


00:44:41.306 --> 00:44:43.183
Okay, kids.
Get out of my way.


00:44:43.308 --> 00:44:47.104
This fence is no match
for my cat-like grace and reflexes.
Here we go.


00:44:49.982 --> 00:44:54.194
Ow. Okay.
Watch me fly, kids.


00:44:59.283 --> 00:45:01.410
Ow!


00:45:01.493 --> 00:45:04.204
I don't think
the little girl's even trying.


00:45:04.288 --> 00:45:08.417
What about your
cat-like... reflexes?


00:45:08.584 --> 00:45:11.795
What about showing a little effort,
shrimp boat? Now, push!


00:45:11.920 --> 00:45:14.214
Whaa!


00:45:14.298 --> 00:45:16.508
All right, Nevins.


00:45:16.592 --> 00:45:18.594
Time to die.


00:45:18.719 --> 00:45:21.805
- Cat, you scared him away!


00:45:21.889 --> 00:45:23.891
Dirty hoe.


00:45:25.601 --> 00:45:29.479
I'm sorry, baby.
I love you. Hmm.


00:45:29.605 --> 00:45:32.316
<i>Come on, Cat!</i>


00:45:36.111 --> 00:45:38.197
There he is!


00:45:40.282 --> 00:45:42.284
<i>Happy birthday, Denise.</i>


00:45:42.409 --> 00:45:44.286
<i>Denise?</i>


00:45:44.495 --> 00:45:47.206
Everyone I know
is there.


00:45:47.289 --> 00:45:49.791
There's Ginny and Alan.


00:45:49.917 --> 00:45:52.794
How come Denise didn't
invite me to her birthday?


00:45:52.920 --> 00:45:55.506
<i>Don't worry. Let’s just
get Nevins and go.</i>


00:45:55.589 --> 00:45:56.715
<i>Okay, kids.
Everyone outside!</i>


00:46:03.388 --> 00:46:05.307
Aaah!


00:46:05.390 --> 00:46:08.602
Nevins.
Cat, get down!
They're gonna see you!


00:46:08.685 --> 00:46:10.979
<i>Hide!</i>


00:46:19.404 --> 00:46:22.282
Piñata! Piñata! Piñata!


00:46:22.407 --> 00:46:24.284
Piñata! Piñata!


00:46:24.409 --> 00:46:27.496
<i>Piñata! Piñata!</i>


00:46:27.579 --> 00:46:30.207
- Everybody join in!


00:46:35.087 --> 00:46:37.089
It's breaking!


00:46:37.214 --> 00:46:40.217
Step out of my way.


00:46:42.719 --> 00:46:44.805
This cannot end well.


00:46:44.888 --> 00:46:47.808
- Piñata! Piñata!


00:46:47.891 --> 00:46:50.018
<i>@¤I'm easy @¤</i>


00:46:50.102 --> 00:46:53.897
<i>@¤Ah, ah, ah, ah @¤</i>


00:46:53.981 --> 00:46:56.608
<i>@¤I'm easy
like Sunday morning @¤@¤</i>


00:47:04.283 --> 00:47:06.618
Oh-ho-ho! Whoo!


00:47:06.702 --> 00:47:09.121
<i>- Oh! Whoo-hoo!
- I got an idea.</i>


00:47:09.204 --> 00:47:11.707
<i>Candy!</i>


00:47:13.292 --> 00:47:15.294
Candy!


00:47:18.297 --> 00:47:21.008
No!


00:47:21.091 --> 00:47:24.386
Get back!
Cat!


00:47:24.511 --> 00:47:26.513
I'll get you!


00:47:30.684 --> 00:47:33.604
I'd love to buy some.


00:47:33.687 --> 00:47:35.814
Hello, Mrs. Kwan.
It’s Joan Walden.


00:47:35.898 --> 00:47:38.400
I just called
to check on the kids.
Are they okay?


00:47:38.484 --> 00:47:41.487
Those aren't children.


00:47:41.612 --> 00:47:44.490
They're little angels.


00:47:46.909 --> 00:47:49.203
That's sweet.


00:47:49.286 --> 00:47:52.206
Well, all right, Mrs. Kwan.
I'll be home as soon as I can.


00:47:52.289 --> 00:47:55.209
Bye-bye.
Bye.


00:48:23.695 --> 00:48:26.782
<i>All right, soldier.
Our bogey is in range.</i>


00:48:26.907 --> 00:48:29.201
Commence
search and destroy.


00:48:29.284 --> 00:48:32.120
<i>- What?
- Search and rescue.</i>


00:48:32.204 --> 00:48:36.583
I meant search and rescue.
Come on!


00:48:36.708 --> 00:48:39.711
I can't believe I wasn't
invited to that party.


00:48:39.795 --> 00:48:42.297
Hey!
You're a lone wolf.


00:48:42.381 --> 00:48:45.008
Live alone, die alone.
Yeah.


00:48:45.092 --> 00:48:48.303
- Can we please get the dog?
Can we please get the dog?


00:48:48.387 --> 00:48:51.306
Can we please get the dog?
Boo!


00:48:54.601 --> 00:48:57.312
<i>Oh, no! Oh, man!</i>


00:48:57.396 --> 00:49:00.315
Hello, Nevins.
Good-bye, Conrad.


00:49:00.399 --> 00:49:04.486
Not so tough now,
are you?


00:49:13.787 --> 00:49:16.498
We're dead.
We're never gonna get
that crate shut.


00:49:16.582 --> 00:49:19.918
<i>And I'm getting shipped off
to Colonel Von Kronk's School
for Wayward Boys!</i>


00:49:20.002 --> 00:49:23.589
Why don't we
take my car?
You have a car?


00:49:23.714 --> 00:49:26.508
<i>Yeah, sure.</i>


00:49:30.888 --> 00:49:33.182
Wow.
That is so cool.


00:49:33.390 --> 00:49:35.809
That's just
the dust cover.


00:49:37.811 --> 00:49:41.982
Here she is, the Super Luxurious
Omnidirectional Whatchamajigger.


00:49:42.107 --> 00:49:44.693
Or S.L.O.W. For short.


00:49:44.818 --> 00:49:46.820
S.L.O.W.?


00:49:46.904 --> 00:49:50.115
Yeah, SLOW.
It's better than the last name we had.


00:49:50.199 --> 00:49:53.410
Super Hydraulic
Instantaneous Transporter.


00:49:53.494 --> 00:49:57.581
- Oh, you mean...
- Ohh! Quick, to the SLOW.


00:50:00.417 --> 00:50:02.294
Buckle up, kids.


00:50:02.294 --> 00:50:06.381
We're on a mission to get that dog,
and we will not rest
until we find and destroy it.


00:50:06.507 --> 00:50:09.009
Rescue it!
Rescue it! Of course
I meant rescue it.


00:50:09.218 --> 00:50:12.513
Whatever. Remember, kids,
there's nothing faster than SLOW.


00:50:12.596 --> 00:50:15.682
That's backwards!
It makes no sense.
Look at you! Argh!


00:50:15.807 --> 00:50:18.393
Okay, here we go.
G.P. S... check.


00:50:18.519 --> 00:50:20.395
<i>DVD, CD... check.</i>


00:50:20.521 --> 00:50:23.482
Someone from Czechoslovakia
is a... Czech.


00:50:23.607 --> 00:50:25.984
Siren!
What are you...
What...


00:50:26.109 --> 00:50:28.403
<i>Siren?</i>


00:50:28.487 --> 00:50:32.282
Let's go!


00:50:32.491 --> 00:50:34.701
Whoo-whoa-ho-ho!


00:50:34.910 --> 00:50:38.205
Hi there!
How are you? Yeah!


00:50:45.212 --> 00:50:50.884
@ I'm sending Conrad away @


00:50:51.009 --> 00:50:53.512
- Oh! Oh!


00:50:53.595 --> 00:50:56.306
<i>Oh!</i>


00:50:56.390 --> 00:50:59.685
I can't believe you whizzed
on my taco!


00:51:02.396 --> 00:51:05.399
Wait till Joan
gets a load of you!


00:51:08.110 --> 00:51:11.280
<i>- There they are!
- Red light, red light,
red light, red light!</i>


00:51:11.405 --> 00:51:13.407
Red light!


00:51:18.120 --> 00:51:21.081
- Someone else should drive.
- All right. You win.


00:51:21.206 --> 00:51:23.709
Concrete,
you drive.
Are you serious?


00:51:23.792 --> 00:51:25.294
I don't know.


00:51:25.294 --> 00:51:29.006
A little voice inside of me
is saying, "This is a bad idea,"


00:51:29.006 --> 00:51:31.008
but I can barely hear
that little voice...


00:51:31.091 --> 00:51:36.305
because an even louder
little voice is screaming,
"Let the 12-year-old drive!"


00:51:36.388 --> 00:51:38.182
Now, punch it!


00:51:40.601 --> 00:51:42.519
<i>This is awesome!</i>


00:51:48.901 --> 00:51:51.904
- I want to drive.
- I think that's a great idea.


00:51:54.907 --> 00:51:57.910
Wait!
Two people can't drive
at the same time.


00:51:57.993 --> 00:52:01.997
You're right.
We should all drive.


00:52:05.501 --> 00:52:09.880
<i>- Cat! Where are the brakes?
- I'll get them.</i>


00:52:12.216 --> 00:52:16.512
I think there's something wrong
with your brakes. When's the
last time you had them checked?


00:52:16.595 --> 00:52:19.681
<i>Bad brake!</i>


00:52:26.980 --> 00:52:30.317
<i>One-way street, one-way street,
one-way street, one-way street!</i>


00:52:35.906 --> 00:52:39.284
Hey, Rhode Island license plate.
You never see those.


00:52:44.498 --> 00:52:47.000
Om. Om.


00:52:53.715 --> 00:52:57.094
Air bag. Standard.


00:52:59.513 --> 00:53:02.307
I think... I wet... my jar.


00:53:02.391 --> 00:53:04.393
Can we do that again?


00:53:11.692 --> 00:53:13.193
Hey, there he is!


00:53:16.280 --> 00:53:18.991
<i>Oh, no!
He's going into Mom's office!</i>


00:53:19.116 --> 00:53:21.410
Come on, Cat!


00:53:23.203 --> 00:53:24.788
You know, Nevins,


00:53:24.913 --> 00:53:28.500
when Joan finds out
you've escaped again,
Conrad will be moving out,


00:53:28.584 --> 00:53:30.586
and I'll be moving in.


00:53:33.088 --> 00:53:36.008
<i> We've gotta get
Nevins and that lock back.
What are we gonna do?</i>


00:53:36.091 --> 00:53:39.303
<i>Don't worry.
I have three plans.</i>


00:53:39.386 --> 00:53:42.389
Plan "A": "Mess up
a perfectly clean house."


00:53:42.514 --> 00:53:47.019
Done that. Plan "B":
"Cut your losses and ditch the kids."


00:53:47.102 --> 00:53:49.688
- That could work.
- What about that one?


00:53:49.813 --> 00:53:54.818
Plan "C": "Trick Mom's boyfriend
into handing over dog and lock."


00:53:54.902 --> 00:53:57.905
I don't know.
I still like Plan "B."


00:53:57.988 --> 00:54:00.699
- Cat!
- Okay, okay. Plan "C."


00:54:00.908 --> 00:54:02.618
Look at you. Argh!


00:54:04.912 --> 00:54:07.498
<i>Excuse me, sir.</i>


00:54:07.581 --> 00:54:10.918
I'd like you to sign
my petition. Yeah.


00:54:11.001 --> 00:54:13.295
Get out of my way,
you hippie freak.


00:54:13.420 --> 00:54:16.089
Are you aware of the senseless,
wholesale slaughter...


00:54:16.215 --> 00:54:19.593
of the flatulating,
acid-spitting Zumzizeroo?


00:54:19.718 --> 00:54:22.221
What will it take
to get you out of my face?


00:54:22.304 --> 00:54:24.515
Just sign my petition...


00:54:24.681 --> 00:54:28.018
with this large, oversized pen
that requires two hands.


00:54:28.101 --> 00:54:30.687
<i>I see.</i>


00:54:30.813 --> 00:54:33.315
- Will you hold my dog?
- Yes!


00:54:33.482 --> 00:54:36.902
Okay, I have a problem
with the word "dog."


00:54:36.985 --> 00:54:40.280
I don't use the "D" word per se
'cause I think it's really, really wrong.


00:54:41.490 --> 00:54:44.993
<i>Yeah. But I will happily
hold your Canine-American.</i>


00:54:45.118 --> 00:54:48.580
- I'm more comfortable
with that really, yeah.


00:54:48.705 --> 00:54:52.793
@ How much is that Canine-American
in the window @


00:54:52.918 --> 00:54:55.420
Cat! Come on!


00:54:57.214 --> 00:54:59.716
<i>- Hey, what the...</i>


00:54:59.800 --> 00:55:02.803
<i>Go, go, go!
Come back here!
I'm on to you kids!</i>


00:55:03.011 --> 00:55:05.806
- Nothing to see here.
Keep moving! Go!


00:55:05.889 --> 00:55:09.017
Come on! Let's go.
Ah, get in, get in!


00:55:09.101 --> 00:55:13.188
Come on, let's go.
Get in! Hi, hi.
Get in! Get in!


00:55:13.397 --> 00:55:16.483
<i>Look out below!</i>


00:55:16.608 --> 00:55:19.820
Oh! Sorry. Over there.


00:55:21.488 --> 00:55:24.491
<i>
Hey! Hey, hey!
Hey, hey!</i>


00:55:24.616 --> 00:55:27.619
<i>Ohh!</i>


00:55:29.913 --> 00:55:32.583
Oh!


00:55:32.708 --> 00:55:34.293
I got you!


00:55:36.503 --> 00:55:39.506
Here he comes!
Cat!


00:55:42.092 --> 00:55:47.181
- Where's my hat? Oh! Go! Go, go!


00:55:47.306 --> 00:55:49.308
Go! Let's go!
My tail, my tail.


00:55:49.391 --> 00:55:53.312
Come on, Cat!
I'm walking here!


00:56:00.110 --> 00:56:03.405
Joan. Joan!


00:56:05.782 --> 00:56:08.702
- I think we lost him.
- Not the pocket. Not the pocket!


00:56:08.785 --> 00:56:12.706
- We got the lock back.
Now let's get home.
- Relax, kid. I'm all over it.


00:56:12.915 --> 00:56:15.501
Hey.


00:56:15.584 --> 00:56:17.711
What's wrong?
This.


00:56:17.794 --> 00:56:20.881
This is not my hat.
I must have picked up
the wrong hat back there.


00:56:21.006 --> 00:56:23.509
- So?
- So...


00:56:23.592 --> 00:56:27.304
without my hat,
I'm just your garden-variety
six-foot-tall talking cat.


00:56:27.596 --> 00:56:28.680
<i>Joan, your children
are running around town
like complete maniacs.</i>


00:56:30.891 --> 00:56:35.521
<i>Yes, they are.
With some weird,
hairy man in a big hat.</i>


00:56:35.604 --> 00:56:37.481
<i>Uh-huh.</i>


00:56:37.606 --> 00:56:40.818
You're gonna believe everything
I'm telling you once we get to
your house, okay? Come on.


00:56:40.901 --> 00:56:42.820
We're doomed!


00:56:42.903 --> 00:56:47.199
We're dead. This is all my fault.
I'm such an idiot.


00:56:47.282 --> 00:56:51.495
Why do I always have to do
the opposite of what I'm supposed to?


00:56:51.620 --> 00:56:53.497
Wait a second.
That's it! The opposite!


00:56:53.705 --> 00:56:57.209
Hey, Things!
Don't help us!


00:56:57.292 --> 00:57:00.879
Do not show up and help us
get home right now!


00:57:01.004 --> 00:57:04.299
- We're goin' on a road trip!
- Larry's car?


00:57:05.592 --> 00:57:08.887
How'd you get so smart?


00:57:09.012 --> 00:57:12.391
<i>
So the race was on
to get back home first.</i>


00:57:12.516 --> 00:57:15.394
Hang on! We gotta beat
Mom and Quinn home!


00:57:15.519 --> 00:57:19.314
<i>But back at their home,
things were just getting worse.</i>


00:57:35.706 --> 00:57:37.499
There's Mom and Larry!


00:57:37.583 --> 00:57:40.711
Step on it, Joan.
Go, go, go, go, go.


00:57:40.794 --> 00:57:45.215
Oh, Things, do not do anything
to slow down my mom.


00:57:45.382 --> 00:57:47.217
<i>Slow down Mom!</i>


00:57:54.183 --> 00:57:57.186
Look, Joan, they don't
beat them every day.


00:57:57.311 --> 00:57:59.605
<i>Oh, great.</i>


00:58:04.693 --> 00:58:07.488
I'm sorry, Officer.
Was I speeding?


00:58:07.613 --> 00:58:10.991
Mekka dekka license,
appa registration.


00:58:12.618 --> 00:58:15.204
Mekka dekka,
you're one hot mama.


00:58:15.287 --> 00:58:17.915
Hey, that's my car.
Joan, we better go right away!


00:58:18.081 --> 00:58:20.292
Please let me handle this.


00:58:20.501 --> 00:58:22.920
Sorry, I guess I was
in a hurry to get home.


00:58:23.003 --> 00:58:26.715
- I'm not gonna let them
get away with this!


00:58:32.095 --> 00:58:33.514
Meet me at the house!


00:58:45.609 --> 00:58:48.612
Not so fast,
you little maggots!
Ha-ha!


00:58:48.695 --> 00:58:52.199
<i>Oh, you are so busted.
Now get inside.</i>


00:58:52.282 --> 00:58:54.284
You don't want to go in there.
It's going to be a total...
Aah!


00:58:56.495 --> 00:58:59.414
What?
Sally, what happened?


00:58:59.498 --> 00:59:01.917
<i>What about the mother
of all messes?
I don't know.</i>


00:59:02.084 --> 00:59:04.711
Why am I sneezing?


00:59:10.509 --> 00:59:13.220
That'd be me. Boo!


00:59:13.303 --> 00:59:16.682
You're a giant...


00:59:16.807 --> 00:59:18.684
Cat!


00:59:22.104 --> 00:59:25.607
Judas Priest!


00:59:25.816 --> 00:59:27.818
<i>Ooh.
Mama mia.</i>


00:59:31.905 --> 00:59:34.283
What happened
to our house?


00:59:34.408 --> 00:59:37.494
It's the mother
of all messes.
Yup!


00:59:37.619 --> 00:59:41.081
Pure, unadulterated fun
without any good sense or judgment.


00:59:41.206 --> 00:59:43.709
See, Corn Dog,
this is why I warned you...


00:59:43.792 --> 00:59:45.711
not to open the crate.


00:59:45.794 --> 00:59:48.505
- Although, on the plus side,


00:59:48.589 --> 00:59:53.302
I think people will be
talking about tonight's party
for the rest of their lives.


00:59:55.596 --> 00:59:58.807
- We gotta shut the crate! Come on!
- Okay.


01:00:01.310 --> 01:00:04.396
Let's take the front hall carpet.


01:00:04.480 --> 01:00:08.400
- This can't be the front hall.
- This is what happens when you
mix your world and my world.


01:00:08.609 --> 01:00:10.903
Oh, and when you eat
bad shellfish.


01:00:10.986 --> 01:00:13.614
Let's go! Oh, yeah!


01:00:13.697 --> 01:00:16.492
Cat, how do we
find the crate?
Beats me.


01:00:16.617 --> 01:00:19.703
This hat is worthless,
and it makes me look fat.


01:00:19.786 --> 01:00:21.914
- Where's Mrs. Kwan?
- Oh-ho-ho!


01:00:21.997 --> 01:00:25.417
<i>Here she comes,
right on schedule.</i>


01:00:27.711 --> 01:00:31.381
- Oh, yeah!
- We're going to ride Mrs. Kwan?


01:00:31.590 --> 01:00:35.219
<i>Sure! It's the only way
to the crate. Hop on!</i>


01:00:35.302 --> 01:00:39.014
Oh, this is gonna be good!


01:00:39.097 --> 01:00:43.018
Please keep your hands and feet
in the Kwan at all times!


01:00:43.101 --> 01:00:47.189
Enjoy the ride!


01:00:47.314 --> 01:00:50.984
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
the dining room. Ohh!</i>


01:00:51.109 --> 01:00:53.403
<i>This is the dining room?</i>


01:00:53.487 --> 01:00:55.697
Hey, look.
Chandelier!


01:01:01.995 --> 01:01:05.207
<i>Is that the bathroom?</i>


01:01:05.290 --> 01:01:07.918
You might want to
hold it for a while.


01:01:10.087 --> 01:01:12.005
Something like that
really burns my...


01:01:12.089 --> 01:01:14.216
Aaah!


01:01:16.093 --> 01:01:21.098
This is amazing!
It's like a ride
at an amusement park!


01:01:21.181 --> 01:01:24.101
You mean, like at...
Universal Studios.


01:01:24.184 --> 01:01:26.812
Cha-ching.


01:01:26.895 --> 01:01:30.607
Whoa!


01:01:33.402 --> 01:01:36.488
- Whoa!


01:01:36.613 --> 01:01:40.701
Please exit the Kwan to your left.
Have a nice day!


01:01:40.784 --> 01:01:43.495
This is ridiculous.
I have to get home.


01:01:43.620 --> 01:01:48.000
Police brutality!
Illegal choke hold!


01:01:49.293 --> 01:01:51.712
Where are we?
The living room,
I think.


01:01:51.795 --> 01:01:54.089
Ah, man!
My eyes are closed.


01:01:54.214 --> 01:01:58.719
If there's no line, could we
go back and do that again?
There's the crate!


01:01:58.802 --> 01:02:00.596
Oh!


01:02:05.809 --> 01:02:07.811
If we shut the crate,
the house will go back to normal.


01:02:07.895 --> 01:02:09.980
You have the lock?


01:02:10.105 --> 01:02:12.399
Got it!
Come on! Let's go!


01:02:15.819 --> 01:02:18.780
Sally!


01:02:18.906 --> 01:02:22.201
- Come on!
- It won't shut!


01:02:22.284 --> 01:02:26.788
Sally! Everything
is disappearing up there!


01:02:26.997 --> 01:02:29.208
- Help!
- Sally!


01:02:29.291 --> 01:02:32.002
- Oh! Oh!
- Sal... Aaah!


01:02:32.085 --> 01:02:34.796
- Help me, Conrad!
- Sally!


01:02:36.381 --> 01:02:40.886
Help me!
I can't hold on!


01:02:41.011 --> 01:02:44.515
Hang on!
Help me, Conrad!


01:02:44.598 --> 01:02:47.684
<i>Help!
Sally, I can't reach
the lock!</i>


01:02:47.810 --> 01:02:51.980
- No!
- I can't save you
unless you let go!


01:02:52.105 --> 01:02:53.899
Okay.


01:02:54.983 --> 01:02:58.403
Help me!


01:02:59.780 --> 01:03:03.283
- Yes!


01:03:31.603 --> 01:03:35.899
<i>Ugh!</i>


01:03:35.983 --> 01:03:38.318
I did it!
I did it!


01:03:38.402 --> 01:03:41.113
<i>I did it! I did it!
I did it!</i>


01:03:41.196 --> 01:03:43.282
I did it! I did it!


01:03:46.493 --> 01:03:50.289
Okay, "we" did it.


01:03:50.414 --> 01:03:53.208
I don't think
we did anything.


01:03:53.417 --> 01:03:57.588
The place is still a wreck.
You said if we shut the crate,
everything would be okay!


01:03:57.713 --> 01:04:00.716
But it's not.
It's a complete disaster!


01:04:00.799 --> 01:04:03.302
Well, what are you
gonna do?


01:04:03.385 --> 01:04:05.304
Tennis, anyone?


01:04:12.811 --> 01:04:15.189
Ooh!


01:04:15.314 --> 01:04:18.108
Love that new ball smell.
Yeah.


01:04:18.192 --> 01:04:23.405
- Hey, your hat... it's magic again?
- Oops.


01:04:23.489 --> 01:04:27.618
Well, now that the cat's out of the bag,
to use an archaic
and cruel-sounding metaphor,


01:04:27.784 --> 01:04:29.703
why don't you serve first?


01:04:29.786 --> 01:04:31.997
You had your real hat
this whole time?


01:04:32.080 --> 01:04:35.292
Uh-yup.
I planned the whole day.


01:04:35.501 --> 01:04:38.921
- What do you mean,
you planned the whole day? All of it?
- Uh-yup.


01:04:39.004 --> 01:04:40.380
- The house getting trashed?
- Uh-yup.


01:04:40.589 --> 01:04:42.216
- Quinn taking Nevins?
- Uh-yup.


01:04:42.299 --> 01:04:45.385
- Cutting off your tail?
- Uh-nope. No.


01:04:46.720 --> 01:04:48.805
<i>You even knew
I'd open the crate?</i>


01:04:48.889 --> 01:04:52.810
Why do you think I made it my one rule?
I knew you couldn't resist.


01:04:52.893 --> 01:04:56.396
Now, who's up for a game
of Canadian doubles?


01:04:59.191 --> 01:05:01.193
Cat, you said nothing bad
would happen.


01:05:01.401 --> 01:05:04.279
Cat, you need to get out.


01:05:04.488 --> 01:05:06.907
I don't know that game.
It's not a game.


01:05:07.115 --> 01:05:10.202
None of this is a game!


01:05:10.285 --> 01:05:14.706
- But I thought you two
wanted to have fun today.
- Look around, Cat.


01:05:14.790 --> 01:05:17.501
<i>You were right.
It's fun to have fun,
but you have to know how.</i>


01:05:17.584 --> 01:05:21.296
You don't know
when enough is enough.
Now, go!


01:05:22.589 --> 01:05:24.383
Suzy.


01:05:24.508 --> 01:05:26.218
Cromwell.


01:05:26.301 --> 01:05:28.220
Please.


01:05:28.303 --> 01:05:30.389
Out!


01:05:37.813 --> 01:05:39.106
Out!


01:05:54.705 --> 01:05:56.790
Good riddance!


01:05:56.915 --> 01:05:59.710
Now, this may not be the time
for “I told you so," but...


01:06:06.300 --> 01:06:08.385
Like I said,
not the time.


01:06:08.510 --> 01:06:10.804
I'll get the mop
and bucket.


01:06:10.888 --> 01:06:14.892
Conrad, you might want
to get out of here until Mom
has a chance to calm down.


01:06:16.310 --> 01:06:19.897
No. This was my fault.
I'll take the blame.


01:06:19.980 --> 01:06:23.400
Look, Mom will be home any second.
Why don't you go upstairs?


01:06:23.484 --> 01:06:25.986
I'm not going upstairs.
I'm staying with you.


01:06:26.111 --> 01:06:29.406
Really? Why?
Two reasons.


01:06:29.490 --> 01:06:31.700
One, the stairs are destroyed.


01:06:31.783 --> 01:06:36.580
Two, this is just as much
my fault as yours.


01:06:36.705 --> 01:06:38.582
We should share the blame.


01:06:39.917 --> 01:06:41.793
Thanks, Sally.


01:06:41.919 --> 01:06:43.795
By the way,


01:06:43.921 --> 01:06:46.298
you're a pretty good brother.


01:06:46.381 --> 01:06:50.385
Glad you think that.
Maybe we can room together
at military school.


01:06:54.181 --> 01:06:57.100
Well, here goes.


01:07:05.818 --> 01:07:08.821
@ Bet you thought I'd gone
Bet you felt a sting @


01:07:08.821 --> 01:07:11.907
<i>@¤Bet you never thought
I'd have another song to sing @¤</i>


01:07:11.990 --> 01:07:14.701
@ But now that you've learned your lesson
Allow me to blow your mind @


01:07:14.785 --> 01:07:17.913
@ By reading to you the small print
of the contract that you signed @@


01:07:17.996 --> 01:07:21.500
Okay, section eight,
article 93, subparagraph 834.


01:07:21.583 --> 01:07:23.502
<i>Right by the chili stain.</i>


01:07:23.585 --> 01:07:27.005
It reads, "If Conrad, a.k.a. Concrete,
should open the crate...


01:07:27.089 --> 01:07:30.300
"and we know he will...
the contract shall be null and void.


01:07:31.802 --> 01:07:33.720
"However,


01:07:33.804 --> 01:07:37.683
if Sally and Conrad
should learn from their mistakes,
the contract shall be reinstated."


01:07:37.808 --> 01:07:40.811
<i>I think you two have satisfied
